### Interfaces — How Agents Connect to Airbyte

Airbyte Agents supports four interfaces. All four support the same capabilities: reading, searching, and taking action across the same cloud-hosted connectors. Connect a data source once in the Airbyte UI, and it's immediately available from every interface.

- [MCP server](https://docs.airbyte.com/ai-agents/interfaces/mcp/): A remote, Airbyte-hosted Model Context Protocol server. One connection gives any MCP-compatible AI agent access to all connected business systems. Endpoint URL: `https://mcp.airbyte.ai/mcp`. Compatible with Claude, Claude Code, ChatGPT, Codex, Cursor, VS Code, and Windsurf. See also: [Airbyte MCP blog post](https://airbyte.com/blog/agent-mcp).
- [Python SDK](https://docs.airbyte.com/ai-agents/interfaces/sdk/): Typed Python library for building agents against Airbyte connectors. Install: `uv add airbyte-agent-sdk` or `pip install airbyte-agent-sdk`. Import: `from airbyte_agent_sdk import connect`. See also: [Agent SDK blog post](https://airbyte.com/blog/agent-sdk).
- [REST API](https://docs.airbyte.com/ai-agents/interfaces/api/): HTTP API for non-Python backends, admin flows, and embedded authentication.
- [Web app](https://docs.airbyte.com/ai-agents/interfaces/ui/): No-code interface at [app.airbyte.ai](https://app.airbyte.ai). Includes Chats (conversational agent sessions) and Automations (scheduled or webhook-triggered agent flows).

### Agent Connectors — 50+ Systems with Read, Search, and Action Capabilities

All agent connectors are cloud-hosted by Airbyte: connect a data source in one click through the Airbyte UI, and it becomes available across every interface (MCP, SDK, API, web app). Every connector exposes a uniform interface: `execute(entity, action, params)`. Read actions include `list`, `get`, `search`, and `context_store_search`. Write/action capabilities include `create`, `update`, and `delete`, available on a growing subset of connectors. New connectors ship weekly. Connectors are also open source: [github.com/airbytehq/airbyte-agent-sdk](https://github.com/airbytehq/airbyte-agent-sdk).

